    {
      "id": "1571641448368185518",
      "type": "Reply",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-15T21:42:00.977+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "Thanks, that clears it up! Re-using signal pads for power works for us. I dug through the run-2 0p5x0p5-cob KiCad files and have a few follow-ups:\n\n1. Will the Run 4 quarter-slot COB board be the same as run-2/0p5x0p5-cob, or is it changing?\n2. Is there a pad-to-net table (which die pads go to VDD_CORE_1, VDD_IO_1/2/3 and the 4 analog lines), or should I read it from the KiCad files?\n3. Is it OK to use several signal pads in parallel for one higher-current node (we'd tie them together on our carrier board)? Any issue with the ESD cells in the default ring when doing that?\n4. What bond wire do you use (gold/aluminum, diameter), and roughly what current per wire do you consider safe?\n5. Is there a max current you'd recommend through one of the 0.1 mm signal traces?\n6. Are the 0201 cap footprints populated by default, and could we pick the values?\n\nThanks again!",
      "author": {
        "id": "913146020798562314",
        "name": "wyomingspopulation",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "uoıʇɐlndoԀsƃuıɯoʎʍ",
        "color": null,
        "isBot": false,
        "roles": [],
        "avatarUrl": "2026-11_media/00500421b32e2f455945bff85cd13884-5C3BC.png"
      },
      "attachments": [],
