    {
      "id": "1571681794732986419",
      "type": "Reply",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-16T00:22:20.3+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "The caps are populated; it's iirc 0.8mil al wire; trace current limits will depend on thermal surroundings.\n\nIf you need/want much more than the reasonable power from the bond wires because you're doing a low-loss switched-mode power converter, you _might_ consider helping working towards qualifying a flip-chip option rated for considerably higher current than the thin wire bonds; there's the `FC01` test dies from Run2; particularly if you have any affordable way (especially there should be a path to scaling it to one-or-more slots of Run4 undergoing the process with their full quantity, post-dicing (||only exception w.r.t. pre/post dicing would be if it's cheap enough and won't conflict with the COB processing for the other slots, in which case doing it pre-dicing might possibly be discussed||)) to plate the existing aluminium pads up in thickness to form bumps which could then via their raised structure define flip-chip bond areas.",
      "author": {
        "id": "262706220073222144",
        "name": "namibj",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "namibj",
        "color": null,
        "isBot": false,
        "roles": [],
        "avatarUrl": "2026-11_media/f885abc0dddd0a33e4d4991b3c99091d-7ACD2.png"
      },
      "attachments": [],
